Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of dietary animal protein on renal stone disease</article-title><source>Nippon Hinyokika Gakkai Zasshi</source><year>1989</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>823</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2552215</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Minich</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bland</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acid-alkaline balance: role in chronic disease and detoxification</article-title><source>Altern Ther Health Med</source><year>2007</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>62</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17658124</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Guenther</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Dodd</surname><given-names>KW</given-names></name><name><surname>Reedy</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Krebs-Smith</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Most Americans eat much less than recommended amounts of fruits and vegetables</article-title><source>J Am Diet Assoc</source><year>2006</year><volume>106</volume><fpage>1371</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16963342</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jada.2006.06.002</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>